  "instance_name": "audience_id",
  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target audience is individuals who hold or are exposed to anti-Latino/Hispanic stereotypes, particularly those who support or are influenced by xenophobic, racist, or Trump administration-aligned rhetoric. The meme is designed to resonate with people who believe in the harmful stereotype that Latinos are inherently desperate, criminal, or willing to risk everything to enter the U.S., especially under a Trump administration. This includes audiences familiar with the U.S.-Mexico border wall imagery and immigration policy debates, and who may be predisposed to viewing Latinos through a lens of moral inferiority or threat. The meme leverages cultural references to Trump’s immigration policies and the visual of border crossing to appeal to those who endorse or are sympathetic to these prejudiced narratives.",
